'''Victor Marx''' (born July 5, 1965) is an American author, minister, and political candidate. He is the [[Republican Party (United States)|Republican]] nominee for [[governor of Colorado]] in the [[2026 Colorado gubernatorial election|2026 election]], where he will face the [[Democratic Party (United States)|Democratic]] nominee [[Phil Weiser]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Luning |first=Ernest |date=May 7, 2026 |title=Victor Marx, Phil Weiser lead Colorado gubernatorial fundraising, as all campaigns' hauls top $20 million |url=https://www.coloradopolitics.com/2026/05/07/victor-marx-phil-weiser-lead-colorado-gubernatorial-fundraising-as-all-campaigns-hauls-top-20-million/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260508170402/https://www.coloradopolitics.com/2026/05/07/victor-marx-phil-weiser-lead-colorado-gubernatorial-fundraising-as-all-campaigns-hauls-top-20-million/ |archive-date=May 8, 2026 |website=Colorado Politics |language=en-US |access-date=May 25, 2026}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.facebook.com/ATPMinistries/posts/-happy-60th-birthday-victor-marx-today-we-celebrate-not-just-a-milestone-but-a-l/1060059306264369/|title=🎉 Happy 60th birthday, Victor Marx! 🎉Today, we celebrate not just a milestone, but a life dedicated to standing for truth, protecting the vulnerable and setting captives free. Here's to many more years of unrelenting passion for the lost, the broken and abused, and all those in captivity.May God continue to bless and guide you in every step of this incredible journey. 🙏|date=July 5, 2025|website=Facebook}}</ref> Marx has made several claims about his life and background that have been seen as sensational and controversial, while the validity of many of his claims has been questioned or disproven.<ref name=":2" /><ref>{{Cite web |first=Seth |last=Klamann |date=August 8, 2026 |title=Once an asset, Victor Marx's extensive backstory becomes uncomfortable talking point in governor's race |url=https://www.denverpost.com/2026/08/08/colorado-victor-marx-governor/ |access-date=September 1, 2026 |website=[[The Denver Post]] |language=en-US}}</ref><ref name=":6">{{Cite news |last=Healy |first=Jack |date=September 29, 2026 |title=Victor Marx, Colorado Governor Nominee With Sensational Past, Splinters the G.O.P. |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2026/09/29/us/victor-marx-colorado-republican-governor-candidate.html |access-date=October 1, 2026 |work=[[The New York Times]] |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref>

== Early life and education ==
Marx was born to a man named Karl Marx<!-- Do not wikilink. His father is not the German philosopher. --> and a young mother<ref>{{Cite web |title=Rare footage of My biological dad Karl Marx (yes it was his name)  He was not the abuse either step father in the film of my life story but rather he was the absent father who didn't originally claim me as his kid.  The story of Reconciliation of our lives later in life is incredible , as he came to faith in Christ Jesus first then me.  He actually got into ministry of working with troubled incarcerated youth and this is a rare video captured of him at 72 yrs old arm wrestling a big youth locked up@for gang affiliation.  My dad sure loved all troubled youth because he was one abd was raised in a boys home at one point in his life.  He was undefeated in arm wrestling these  young men but got their respect in order to share the Truth of Christ Jesus .  I miss him but am happy for him being in heaven for many years now. |url=https://www.instagram.com/reel/CP8wbt2pNK6/ |website=Instagram |language=en-US |date=June 10, 2021 |access-date=May 29, 2026}}</ref><ref name="PBS Hawai'i 2015">{{Cite web |last=PBS Hawai'i |date=June 16, 2015 |title=Victor Marx {{!}} Long Story Short with Leslie Wilcox |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=y15GxS618eA |website=YouTube |language=en-US |access-date=May 29, 2026}}</ref> in [[Lafayette, Louisiana]], where he also grew up.<ref>{{Cite web |last= |first= |date=April 5, 2018 |title=Child abuse survivor shares his story with News 5 |url=https://www.koaa.com/news/2018/04/05/child-abuse-survivor-shares-his-story-with-news-5/ |website=KOAA News 5 |language=en-US |access-date=May 29, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260529231552/https://www.koaa.com/news/2018/04/05/child-abuse-survivor-shares-his-story-with-news-5/ |archive-date=May 29, 2026 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="Markus 2026a">{{Cite web |last=Markus |first=Ben |date=May 20, 2026 |title=Colorado GOP governor primary pits MAGA candidates against establishment favorite |url=https://www.cpr.org/2026/05/20/colorado-gop-governor-primary-candidates/ |website=Colorado Public Radio |language=en-US |access-date=May 25, 2026}}</ref><ref name="PBS Hawai'i 2015"/> He has three older siblings, the first of whom was born when Marx's mother was 16.<ref name="PBS Hawai'i 2015"/> Marx says he is a survivor of [[child abuse]].<ref name="Luning 2025">{{Cite web |last=Luning |first=Ernest |date=October 3, 2025 |title=Ministry founder, 'high-risk' missionary Victor Marx joins Colorado's Republican gubernatorial primary |url=https://www.coloradopolitics.com/2025/10/03/ministry-founder-high-risk-missionary-victor-marx-joins-colorados-republican-gubernatorial-primary/ |website=Colorado Politics |access-date=May 30, 2026}}</ref> Marx claimed that, when he was three years old, his stepfather forced him to behead a cat and wear its carcass on his head.<ref name="Corn 2026">{{Cite web |last=Corn |first=David |authorlink=David Corn |date=July 15, 2026 |title=The most extreme GOP candidate in the nation |url=https://www.motherjones.com/politics/2026/07/victor-marx-colorado-governor-candidate-republican-gop-extreme-murder/ |website=[[Mother Jones (magazine)|Mother Jones]] |language=en-US |access-date=July 22, 2026}}</ref> As a child, Marx moved frequently, living in 17 different homes and attending 14 different schools.<ref name="PBS Hawai'i 2015"/>

Marx alleged that at age seven, his abusive stepfather drove him at night to a rural area of [[Mendenhall, Mississippi]], and made him shoot and kill a man. Mississippi sheriffs and police in the area have said there is no record of any unsolved homicides from that time. Marx claimed he contacted the [[Federal Bureau of Investigation]] and the local sheriff's office, neither of which could solve the case as Marx was unable to provide many details. There is no evidence that Marx ever contacted authorities.<ref name="Markus 2026a"/> Marx mentioned in an interview with Colorado news station [[KUSA (TV)|9News]] that he is unsure how many people he has killed, and that he thinks the exact details do not need to be clarified.<ref name=":1">{{Cite web |date=May 27, 2026 |title=Full interview: Colorado Republican gubernatorial candidate Victor Marx |url=https://www.9news.com/video/news/politics/full-interview-colorado-republican-gubernatorial-candidate-victor-marx/73-c7e83d54-e098-41c0-b4fb-15457b261b06 |website=[[KUSA (TV)|9News]] |language=en-US |access-date=May 29, 2026}}</ref>

== Career ==
He served for three years in the [[United States Marine Corps]] from 1983 to 1986. He was inspired to do so after the [[1983 Beirut barracks bombings]].<ref name="Markus 2026a" /><ref>{{Cite web |date=2016-05-26 |title=Marine turned missionary campaigns to strengthen resiliency, readiness |url=https://www.army.mil/article/168730/marine_turned_missionary_campaigns_to_strengthen_resiliency_readiness |access-date=2026-05-29 |website=www.army.mil}}</ref> Towards the end of his service in the Marine Corps, Marx reunited with his biological father, who spurred his conversion to Christianity.<ref name="Biddle & Poulson 2023">{{Cite web |last=Biddle |first=Sam |last2=Poulson |first2=Jack |date=July 29, 2023 |title=The Online Christian Counterinsurgency Against Sex Workers |url=https://theintercept.com/2023/07/29/skull-games-surveillance-sex-workers/ |website=[[The Intercept]] |language=en-US |access-date=July 22, 2026|author-link=Sam Biddle}}</ref> Marx was an assistant for three years at [[James Dobson]]'s [[Evangelical Christian]] organization [[Focus on the Family]].<ref name="Markus 2026a" />

Marx founded All Things Possible Ministries in 2003.<ref name="Biddle & Poulson 2023" /> Marx claimed on his campaign website that All Things Possible rescued 45,000 women and children from abuse, which was later removed from his campaign website after being disproved.<ref>{{Cite news |last1=Wright |first1=David |last2=Iyer |first2=Kaanita |date=July 9, 2026 |title=Victor Marx, a self-described 'high-risk humanitarian,' will win GOP nomination for Colorado governor, CNN projects |url=https://www.cnn.com/2026/07/09/politics/victor-marx-colorado-republican-nominee-governor |work=[[CNN]] |language=en-US |access-date=July 21, 2026}}</ref><ref name="Corn 2026" /> Marx has since declined to give an exact number of survivors saved in order to not "put people in danger".<ref name="Corn 2026" /><ref name=":1" />

As part of his ministry, Marx has said that he routinely encountered and [[Exorcism|exorcised]] demons from people,<ref>{{cite web|last=Walker|first=Hunter|url=https://talkingpointsmemo.com/news/colorado-gop-gov-nominee-claims-to-have-battled-demons-with-reptilian-eyes|title=Colorado GOP Gov Nominee Claims to Have Battled 'Demons' With 'Reptilian' Eyes|website=[[Talking Points Memo]]|date=August 21, 2026}}</ref> including from individuals he claimed were [[Spirit possession|possessed]] due to the influence of [[pornography]] or being an unmarried couple living together.<ref>{{Cite web |last1=Klamann |first1=Seth |date=July 10, 2026 |title=Victor Marx, the Republican nominee for Colorado governor, has an unusual backstory. Here's what to know. |url=https://www.denverpost.com/2026/07/10/victor-marx-gop-nomination-colorado-governor/ |website=[[The Denver Post]] |language=en-US |access-date=July 22, 2026}}</ref><ref name="Corn 2026"/> These exorcisms were sometimes done over the phone.<ref name=":2">{{Cite web |last=Frank |first=John |date=August 10, 2026 |title=What we know and don't about Victor Marx, the Republican governor candidate in Colorado |url=https://www.axios.com/local/denver/2026/08/10/victor-marx-colorado-governor-what-to-know |website=[[Axios (website)|Axios]] |language=en-US |access-date=August 17, 2026}}</ref> On a 2023 episode of [[Alex Clark (commentator)|Alex Clark]]'s podcast, he claimed that he "hunts demons" and recalled a time when his dog supposedly identified a demonic presence in a couple resting at a pool, where he claims he then exorcised the woman from "five demons that had been assigned to her".<ref name="Corn 2026" /><ref name="Klamann 2026a"/>

Marx was reportedly friends with conservative political commentator [[Charlie Kirk]]. He was a guest on an episode of Kirk's podcast in 2022,<ref name="Corn 2026" /> and has spoken at many [[Turning Point USA]] events.<ref>{{Cite web |last=McAlindin |first=Sean |date=May 8, 2026 |title=GOP candidate for Colorado governor Victor Marx to visit Grand County |url=https://www.skyhinews.com/news/gop-candidate-for-colorado-governor-victor-marx-visits-snow-mountain-ranch/ |website=Sky-Hi News |language=en-US |access-date=May 30, 2026}}</ref>

== 2026 Colorado gubernatorial campaign ==
On October 1, 2025, he announced his campaign for governor of Colorado.<ref>{{Cite news |date=October 1, 2025 |title=Colorado Springs ministry leader announces run for governor |url=https://www.9news.com/video/news/local/next/next-with-kyle-clark/colorado-springs-ministry-leader-announces-run-for-governor/73-c7df2819-59d8-4d74-ad90-e08e8e1e6ed2 |work=[[KUSA (TV)|9News]] |language=en-US |access-date=July 22, 2026}}</ref> Marx has said that his wife encouraged him to do so.<ref name="Markus 2026a"/> He ran in the Republican primary for the [[2026 Colorado gubernatorial election]] against state senator [[Barbara Kirkmeyer]] and state representative [[Scott Bottoms]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Dolven |first=Taylor |date=April 12, 2026 |title=State Rep. Scott Bottoms secures top spot on Republican primary ballot for Colorado governor |url=https://coloradosun.com/2026/04/11/scott-bottoms-gop-primary-ballot-colorado-governor/ |website=[[The Colorado Sun]] |language=en-US |access-date=May 25, 2026}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=2026 Primary Election Petition Candidates Who Submitted Petition Signatures |url=https://www.coloradosos.gov/pubs/elections/vote/primaryPetitionCandidates.html |publisher=[[Colorado Secretary of State]] |language=en-US |access-date=May 25, 2026}}</ref> Marx won nearly 40% of the vote at the Republican state assembly in April 2026.<ref name="Coltrain 2026">{{Cite web |last1=Coltrain |first1=Nick |date=May 26, 2026 |title=Victor Marx might be leading the GOP race for Colorado governor. But he's skipping most debates. |url=https://www.denverpost.com/2026/05/26/victor-marx-republican-governor-race-debates/ |website=[[The Denver Post]] |language=en-US |access-date=May 30, 2026}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last1=Klamann |first1=Seth |date=April 11, 2026 |title=Conservative pastor Rep. Scott Bottoms wins top billing for governor on Colorado Republican primary ballot |url=https://www.denverpost.com/2026/04/11/colorado-scott-bottoms-republican-primary/ |website=[[The Denver Post]] |language=en-US |access-date=May 30, 2026}}</ref> Marx's campaign has received $2.5 million in donations, more than Kirkmeyer's and Bottoms's campaigns combined.<ref name="Markus 2026a"/> Marx skipped many of the Republican debates during his campaign, a decision that Paul Teske, a professor of public affairs at the [[University of Colorado Denver]], called "unusual". Marx originally agreed to attend a debate on May 26, 2026. However, one of the debate moderators, [[KOA (AM)|KOA NewsRadio]] host Michael Brown, sent Marx a long list of claims he requested Marx prove. These claims included ministry work in the Middle East and Haiti, a gun battle with [[ISIS]], and his martial arts credentials.<ref name="Coltrain 2026"/> Marx rejected Brown's request, calling it "a staged ambush disguised as a debate", and instead held a counter-rally to the debate.<ref name="Coltrain 2026"/> During the primary campaign, Kirkmeyer and Bottoms criticized Marx for avoiding debates.<ref name="Luning 2026">{{Cite web |last=Luning |first=Ernest |date=May 27, 2026 |title=Republicans Kirkmeyer, Bottoms say they won't back Marx if he wins Colorado's gubernatorial primary |url=https://www.coloradopolitics.com/2026/05/27/republicans-kirkmeyer-bottoms-say-they-wont-back-marx-if-he-wins-colorados-gubernatorial-primary/ |website=Colorado Politics |language=en-US |access-date=July 21, 2026}}</ref>

Marx was questioned about his past claims in an interview with 9News anchor Kyle Clark in June 2026. He denied claiming to have performed "more than 130 missions" in 30 countries rescuing women and children or to have called in an airstrike as a civilian that killed 70 ISIS fighters.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Littwin |first1=Mike |date=June 2, 2026 |title=Littwin: Victor Marx's interview with Kyle Clark likely to win him MAGA votes |url=https://coloradosun.com/2026/05/31/littwin-victor-marx-kyle-clark-interview-wins-maga-votes/ |website=[[The Colorado Sun]] |language=en-US |access-date=July 16, 2026}}</ref>

Leading to the June primary, Kirkmeyer and Bottoms indicated they would refuse to endorse Marx if he won the GOP nomination. Kirkmeyer believed he was unfit to be governor and a "disaster for our state", while Bottoms said that Marx was a "con man".<ref name="Luning 2026"/> Marx narrowly won the June 30 Republican primary with the race called about a week later on July 9, and will face Democratic candidate and [[Colorado Attorney General]] [[Phil Weiser]] in the November general election.<ref name=":0">{{cite web |last1=Konig |first1=Joseph |date=July 10, 2026 |title=Self-Dubbed 'High Risk Humanitarian,' Who Claims He Killed a Man at Age 7, Wins Colorado's GOP Governor Race: Inside His Wildest Claims |url=https://people.com/victor-marx-claims-colorado-governor-election-12016150 |website=[[People (magazine)|People]] |language=en-US |access-date=July 16, 2026}}</ref>

Soon after Marx was declared the GOP nominee, he circulated a loyalty pledge so the other Republican candidates can sign to indicate their support for his campaign.<ref>{{Cite news |date=July 13, 2026 |title=Victor Marx asks Republicans to sign loyalty pledges |url=https://www.9news.com/article/news/politics/victor-marx-republicans-loyalty-pledges/73-af274fa3-aecc-40a5-b110-a3ca2de4a6ae |work=9News |language=en-US |access-date=21 July 2026}}</ref> As of July 15, most of the statewide Republican candidates had not publicly signed the pledge.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Luning |first=Ernest |date=July 16, 2026 |title=Republican candidates pass on signing Colorado gubernatorial nominee Victor Marx's 'unity compact' |url=https://www.coloradopolitics.com/2026/07/15/republican-candidates-pass-on-signing-colorado-gubernatorial-nominee-victor-marxs-unity-compact/ |website=Colorado Politics |language=en-US |access-date=July 22, 2026}}</ref> On July 15, Marx claimed in a talk radio show that former Republican governor [[Bill Owens (Colorado politician)|Bill Owens]] endorsed him in the Governor's race, saying "I got a call yesterday that he's endorsing me". In a statement, Owens responded that he has not officially endorsed Marx, saying he intends to wait to see how Marx's campaign unfolds.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Paul |first=Jesse |date=July 16, 2026 |title=Victor Marx says he's being endorsed by Colorado's last Republican governor. That's not true — yet. |url=https://coloradosun.com/2026/07/15/victor-marx-bill-owens-endorsement-discrepancy/ |website=[[The Colorado Sun]] |language=en-US |access-date=July 22, 2026}}</ref> Marx's candidacy has led to tensions within the state GOP, with several Republicans refusing to support Marx's campaign while others urging the party to back Marx.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Birkeland · |first=Bente |date=2026-08-18 |title=Colorado Republicans were already divided. Then Victor Marx got nominated |url=https://www.cpr.org/2026/08/18/victor-marx-colorado-republicans-divided/ |access-date=2026-09-01 |website=[[Colorado Public Radio]] |language=en}}</ref><ref name=":6" /> In late July, Marx selected Marine veteran George Markert as his running mate.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Paul |first=Jesse |date=July 31, 2026 |title=Victor Marx selects fellow Marine veteran as running mate in Colorado governor's race |url=https://coloradosun.com/2026/07/31/victor-marx-george-markert-running-mate-colorado-governors-race/ |access-date=September 21, 2026 |website=[[The Colorado Sun]] |language=en-US}}</ref>

Marx's campaign has faced several allegations of breaking [[campaign finance law]]s.<ref name=":6" /><ref name=":5">{{Cite web |last=Woodruff |first=Chase |date=September 4, 2026 |title=Republican Victor Marx faces fine over 'unprecedented' campaign finance violations |url=https://coloradonewsline.com/2026/09/04/victor-marx-faces-fine-campaign-finance-violations/ |access-date=September 21, 2026 |website=Colorado Newsline |language=en-US}}</ref> On July 27, Marx's campaign was alleged to have violated state campaign finance laws according to state election officials, and was accused of accepting over 100 improper contributions during the primary election that exceeded the legal amount.<ref name="Klamann 2026b">{{Cite web |last=Klamann |first=Seth |date=July 27, 2026 |title=Victor Marx's campaign accepted more than $78,000 in improper donations, Colorado election officials allege |url=https://www.denverpost.com/2026/07/27/victor-marx-campaign-finance-allegations-governor/ |website=[[The Denver Post]] |language=en-US |access-date=August 17, 2026}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Birkeland |first=Bente |date=July 24, 2026 |title=Victor Marx dinged for campaign finance violations |url=https://www.cpr.org/2026/07/24/victor-marx-campaign-finance-violations/ |website=[[Colorado Public Radio]] |language=en-US |access-date=August 18, 2026}}</ref> Marx's campaign said they were working with state officials on the matter, while Marx called the violations a "nothing burger".<ref name="Klamann 2026b"/><ref name=":9">{{Cite news |date=July 31, 2026 |title=Victor Marx soliciting unlimited donations despite campaign finance limits |url=https://www.9news.com/article/news/politics/elections/victor-marx-soliciting-unlimited-donations-despite-campaign-finance-limits/73-104f369b-640d-41ca-a887-0579462e051a |work=[[KUSA (TV)|9News]] |language=en-US |access-date=August 17, 2026}}</ref> In a September hearing with election officials, Marx's campaign admitted to accepting improper contributions and not fully refunding the excess amount along with failing to provide adequate evidence for completed refunds.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Birkeland |first=Bente |date=September 14, 2026 |title=Victor Marx campaign finance complaint testimony wraps up |url=https://www.cpr.org/2026/09/14/victor-marx-campaign-finance-testimony-finishes/ |access-date=September 21, 2026 |website=[[Colorado Public Radio]] |language=en}}</ref> The campaign will face a fine which may be as much as $420,000.<ref>{{Cite news |date=18 September 2026 |title=Political Updates: Marx could be fined $420,000, key ballot measure could be in danger |url=https://www.cbsnews.com/colorado/video/political-updates-marx-could-be-fined-420000-key-ballot-measure-could-be-in-danger/ |access-date=21 September 2026 |work=[[CBS News Colorado]]}}</ref>

In late July, Marx announced to his supporters that they can buy campaign merchandise via a new website to bypass campaign finance restrictions on individuals donating more than $3,500 to a single campaign. During an online campaign event, Marx said "If they order merchandise, there's no limit on that. They can order as much as they want. That will really help us."<ref name=":9" /> [[KUSA (TV)|9News]] reported that the new online store directly links through Marx's official campaign website, that the merchandise on the new store mirrors items found in the official campaign website and that the site does not mention typical campaign donation disclosures.<ref name=":9" /> According to several campaign finance experts contacted by 9News, it may be legally dubious whether it complies with campaign finance laws and raises uncertainty whether the money is going to Marx's campaign, to himself, or to another group.<ref name=":9" /> On August 14, state election officials notified Marx's campaign that they found "one or more potential violations of Colorado campaign and political finance law" that need be fixed by the end of the month or potentially face fines.<ref>{{Cite news |first1=Kyle |last1=Clark |first2=Angela |last2=Case |date=August 16, 2026 |title=Victor Marx faces deadline to fix potential campaign finance violations |url=https://www.9news.com/article/news/local/local-politics/colorado-elections-division-victor-marx-deadline-campaign-finance-violations/73-73412269-8f5a-4076-803c-d3c5105dfa8d |work=[[KUSA (TV)|9News]] |language=en-US |access-date=August 17, 2026}}</ref> Around August 28, the website became inaccessible and Marx denied involvement, saying "I don't have anything to do with it" when contacted about the website by 9News.<ref>{{Cite news |first=Kyle |last=Clark |date=28 August 2026 |title=Victor Marx denies pocketing campaign merchandise cash, says financial filing was a 'silly mistake' |url=https://www.9news.com/article/news/politics/victor-marx-denies-pocketing-campaign-merchandise/73-22b81c19-fcf6-41f0-9a5e-038708081dbf |access-date=1 September 2026 |work=[[KUSA (TV)|9News]]}}</ref> Complaints were sent to election officials over the alleged violations and were reportedly under review as of early September.<ref name=":5" /> On October 2, a hearing officer determined that Marx owed $57,000 for campaign finance violations.<ref name=":7">{{Cite web |last=Moore |first=Marilyn |date=October 2, 2026 |title=Hearing officer recommends $57K fine for GOP governor nominee Victor Marx for campaign finance violations |url=https://www.9news.com/article/news/politics/colorado-republican-victor-marx-campaign-fined/73-23238e12-378d-41b7-9435-0dd7f5f7f7dd |website=[[KUSA (TV)|9News]]}}</ref>  That decision goes to the Secretary of State for a final decision.<ref name=":7" />

== Political positions ==
[[David Corn]] of [[Mother Jones (magazine)|''Mother Jones'']] has described Marx as a [[Christian fundamentalism|Christian fundamentalist]].<ref name="Corn 2026"/> Some political observers, including other Republicans, have voiced criticism that Marx has generally avoided giving specifics on policies and has not discussed such matters in detail.<ref name="Klamann 2026a">{{Cite web |last1=Klamann |first1=Seth |date=June 11, 2026 |title=Victor Marx's atypical campaign for governor — and sometimes-incredible backstory — makes him a force in GOP primary |url=https://www.denverpost.com/2026/06/11/victor-marx-colorado-governor-race-profile/ |website=[[The Denver Post]] |language=en-US |access-date=July 21, 2026}}</ref> During the primary, Marx stated he intentionally avoided detailed policy discussions, saying that voters should focus on his background instead.<ref name="Klamann 2026a"/> According to a ''[[Colorado Newsline]]'' article, "Along with debates, Marx has largely eschewed offering specifics about the policy agenda he would pursue as governor, decrying the 'empty promises' made by too many politicians on the campaign trail".<ref name=":4">{{Cite web |last=Woodruff |first=Chase |date=June 3, 2026 |title=Kirkmeyer, Bottoms blast Victor Marx as 'unfit' and 'corrupt' during GOP gubernatorial debate |url=https://sentinelcolorado.com/state-and-region-news/colorado-news-state-and-region-news/kirkmeyer-bottoms-blast-victor-marx-as-unfit-and-corrupt-during-gop-gubernatorial-debate/ |website=Sentinel Colorado |language=en-US |access-date=July 21, 2026}}</ref>

Marx has said if elected as Colorado governor he would cut regulations to expand housing and [[Child care|childcare]], as well as increasing energy production to lower gas and utility costs. He has stated a commitment to protecting [[TABOR]] in Colorado.<ref name="Markus 2026b">{{Cite web |last=Markus |first=Ben |date=May 29, 2026 |title=Colorado Gubernatorial Candidate: Republican Victor Marx |url=https://www.cpr.org/2026/05/29/vg-2026-primary-election-colorado-governor-victor-marx/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260602214457/https://www.cpr.org/2026/05/29/vg-2026-primary-election-colorado-governor-victor-marx/ |archive-date=June 2, 2026 |website=[[Colorado Public Radio]] |language=en-US |access-date=May 29, 2026}}</ref> On affordability issues, ''Colorado Newsline'' reported that Marx offered a "vague answer" to moderators during a debate then elaborated that he would "negotiate with people to accomplish a greater good."<ref name=":4" /> Marx has proposed a pause on regulations and a cap on property taxes.<ref name=":4" />

Marx strongly supports the [[Second Amendment to the United States Constitution|Second Amendment]]. As Colorado governor, he has said that he would codify Second Amendment rights directly into the [[Colorado State Constitution]] in case the federal Second Amendment may be altered.<ref name="KREX News 2026">{{Cite web |publisher=KREX News 5 |date=May 12, 2026 |title=Exclusive interview with Victor Marx: Talking about the Gubernatorial election |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pdive6ixdKY |website=YouTube |language=en-US |access-date=May 30, 2026}}</ref>

Marx opposes [[Flock Safety]] cameras.<ref name="KREX News 2026"/>

In spite of Colorado laws prohibiting such a policy, Marx has stated he wants to cooperate with federal immigration enforcement, such as [[United States Immigration and Customs Enforcement|ICE]].<ref name="Markus 2026a"/><ref name="Markus 2026b"/> He intends to oppose [[sanctuary city]] policies and establish a "Border-Related Crime Strike Force".<ref name="Markus 2026b"/> Marx endeavors to launch task forces on [[fentanyl]] and [[trafficking]] networks.<ref name="Markus 2026a" />

Marx strongly opposes [[Abortion in the United States|abortion]]. On August 2026, Marx compared abortion to "[[spiritual warfare]]" and said about Colorado's abortion protections: "This state, they kill babies. Wholesale slaughter."<ref name=":3">{{Cite journal |last=Beedle |first=Sean |date=2026-08-31 |title=Dems Warn Marx has 'the Most Extreme Position on Abortion' |url=https://coloradotimesrecorder.com/2026/08/dems-warn-marx-has-the-most-extreme-position-on-abortion/81350/ |journal=Colorado Times Recorder |language=en-US |publisher=}}</ref> Marx's running mate George Markert has said that he and Marx will attempt to eliminate abortion protections in the state if elected.<ref name=":3" />

== Personal life ==
Marx has five children and five grandchildren.<ref name="Luning 2025"/> Marx met his wife Eileen through a mutual interest in [[martial arts]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=Victor and Eileen Marx |url=https://lifetoday.org/life-today-tv/guest-directory/victor-marx/ |website=Life Today |language=en-US |date=March 29, 2019 |access-date=May 25, 2026}}</ref> Eileen is a fitness [[kickboxer]]. Following their marriage, they opened a gym. A pastor in [[Honolulu]] enticed Marx and his wife to move there to start a Christian [[karate]] school. Marx spent many years in Hawaii, living there from 1995 to 2001. He began feeling suicidal, and he checked himself into [[The Queen's Medical Center]]. While living in Honolulu, his children learned [[Hawaiian Pidgin]].<ref name="PBS Hawai'i 2015"/>

In 2023, Marx's brother-in-law, Kenneth Breining, shot at Marx from inside the trailer he was living in on Marx's property. Marx was not hit. Breining was taken to an [[El Paso County, Colorado|El Paso County]] jail and later bonded out. In 2024, Breining was suspected of murdering his girlfriend in [[Nevada County, California]], where he remains in jail.<ref name="Markus 2026a"/><ref>{{cite web |last1=Egel |first1=Benjy |date=April 14, 2024 |title=Nevada City man, 64, suspected of killing his girlfriend before trying to take own life |url=https://amp.sacbee.com/news/local/crime/article287673650.html |website=[[The Sacramento Bee]] |language=en-US |access-date=July 14, 2026}}</ref>

Inspired by the 1983 [[Chuck Norris]] film ''[[Lone Wolf McQuade]]'', Marx has posted [[social media]] videos in which he disarms people holding dummy firearms.<ref name="Markus 2026b"/>

In 2026, controversial recordings of Marx on a podcast with [[Byron Rodgers]] resurfaced wherein he talked about slamming his wife into the front door of their home, giving her a "decent, bouncing push," that led to her "bent over, ...crying." A second recording from Marx's own podcast in 2020 also resurfaced, wherein he discussed a past incident in which he "snatched up and threw [his toddler son] across the room." Marx described himself as feeling as though "God gave [Marx] a gift for violence," in a third recording from a 2023 [[Turning Point USA]] Pastors Summit.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Napiza |first1=Chelsie |date=October 1, 2026 |title='She Bent Over and Started Crying': Colorado GOP Nominee Laughs Recalling Slamming His Wife Into a Door |url=https://www.ibtimes.co.uk/victor-marx-recordings-violence-colorado-governor-race-1823105 |website=[[International Business Times UK]] |language=en-US |access-date=October 20, 2026}}</ref>

